# EtAnimatedCount

## Purpose & Scope

`EtAnimatedCount` renders a number (or pre-formatted string) as a row of individually animated digit
slots. Digits animate with a spring "odometer" by default, formatting characters (commas, decimals,
currency symbols) stay static, and the whole row can reflow smoothly as the value's length changes.

- **Digit anchoring**: `'decimal'` (default) anchors identity to the decimal point so live-updating
  magnitudes (prices, balances) roll in place like an odometer; `'leading'` anchors to typed order so a
  freshly typed digit drops in from a blank slot on the right (numeric input).
- **Static fallback**: `disableAnimation` renders `StaticDigit`/`StaticCharacter` (no animation) for
  focus/scrubbing modes.

> Structured after the canonical `components/button` role model (see `building-ui-components.mdc`):
> a dedicated `animations/` folder holds every animated style/builder, `hooks/` is logic-only, `api/`
> holds types, `subcomponents/` holds the render bricks, and `utils/` holds pure parsers.

## File Structure

```
animated-digits/
├── api/                    # Types (index.ts re-exports types.ts)
├── animations/             # ANIMATION_CONFIG + entering/layout builders + useOdometerAnimation
├── hooks/                  # use-animated-count-config (derivation) + use-animated-count-state (timing)
├── subcomponents/          # animated-digits, leading-digit-cell, odometer-column, static-character, static-digit
├── utils/                  # pure: character-parser, character-keys, init-props (+ specs)
├── constants.ts            # ANIMATED_COUNT_DEFAULTS (non-animation)
├── styles.ts               # static row container style
├── et-animated-count.tsx   # composition-only: config -> state -> render
├── index.ts                # barrel (public: EtAnimatedCount)
└── AGENTS.mdc
```

`et-animated-count.tsx` is composition-only: it calls `useAnimatedCountConfig` -> `useAnimatedCountState`,
builds `commonProps`, and maps parsed characters to the right subcomponent. All springs/layout builders
live in `animations/`; all derivation (formatting, parsing, keys, text style) lives in `hooks/`.

## Entry Point

```tsx
<EtAnimatedCount
  number={1234.56}          // number | string (pre-formatted passes through)
  digitAnchor="decimal"     // 'decimal' (odometer) | 'leading' (typed input)
  disableAnimation={false}  // static render for scrub/focus
  fontSize={50}
  color={colors.textPrimaryNeutral}
/>
```

## Notes

- Public API is only `EtAnimatedCount` (exported from `src/index.ts`); everything else is internal.
- Animation builders are worklet-safe and created once at module scope where possible to avoid per-render
  reallocation (`makeRoomTransition`, `buildDropInEntering`).
